title: "Helene Storymap"
abstract: "This cookbook is a combination of four contributors and their efforts to tell the story of Helene, a major hurricane that impacted the Southeast United States in 2024. First, an overview of its genesis, intensification, and storm surge impacts on Florida are reviewed. Next, its landfall and extratropical transition, as well as its cyclone phase space is analyzed as the storm decays. Then, rain gauges, tide gauges, and landslide reports are gathered in North Carolina to assess the severity of inland flooding. Finally, the societal vulnerability prior to Helene was assessed in the Appalachian region through vulnerability indices and socioeconomic data. We want to cover the meteorology behind how hurricanes form and intensify, their detrimental impacts, and highlight the need for better observational networks and protection for vulnerable populations in advance of life changing severe weather events."
